Q: Is there a way to restrict snippets to work under certain path A: <p><code>include</code> and <code>exclude</code> were recently added to vscode snippet's options: <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/284165" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Add glob pattern filter settings to snippets</a>.  So you could do something like this in your snippets file:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>
  &quot;Print to console&quot;: {
    // &quot;scope&quot;: &quot;javascript&quot;,       // not necessary with the following include option
    &quot;include&quot;: &quot;**/main/Folder1/*.js&quot;,
    &quot;prefix&quot;: &quot;srr&quot;,

    &quot;body&quot;: [
      &quot;&lt;$0&gt;${TM_SELECTED_TEXT}&lt;/&gt;&quot;,
    ]
  }
</code></pre>
<p>and then <code>&quot;include&quot;: &quot;**/main/Folder2/*.js&quot;,</code> for other folder snippets.</p>
<p><code>include/exclude</code> can use <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/glob-patterns" rel="nofollow noreferrer">globs </a> as values.</p>

Q: Get decimal portion of a number with JavaScript A: <p>Here is another approach to achieve &quot;Getting Fractional Part of Number in js&quot;:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const fractionCount = (number)=&gt;{
    let count = 0;
    while(number !== Math.floor(number)){
        number*=10;
        count++;        
    }
    return count;    
}

console.log(fractionCount(2.3456790))</code></pre>
